    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.92,
      "end_seconds": 12.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.7,
      "end_seconds": 22.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "It's, It's a weak urine stream. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.04,
      "end_seconds": 27.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Okay, how many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.66,
      "end_seconds": 34.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "About... well, one week. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.39,
      "end_seconds": 38.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.89,
      "end_seconds": 41.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.74,
      "end_seconds": 45.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.93,
      "end_seconds": 58.24,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "Dribbling after passing urine goes along with it, most of the time. The dribbling after passing urine? That's been for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.83,
      "end_seconds": 61.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Has there been any back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.26,
      "end_seconds": 65.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Not at all, no back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.52,
      "end_seconds": 73.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "A few quick ones: weight loss, burning on passing urine or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.08,
      "end_seconds": 86.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "I haven't had weight loss, burning on passing urine or blood in the urine, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.98,
      "end_seconds": 91.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.63,
      "end_seconds": 95.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Yeah, I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.44,
      "end_seconds": 102.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.74,
      "end_seconds": 123.63,
      "duration_seconds": 20.89,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I have about eight cigarettes in a day. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.56,
      "end_seconds": 136.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.78,
      "end_seconds": 145.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.91,
      "text": "Um, I was told I'm allergic to erythromycin, but I don't remember what reaction I had."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.85,
      "end_seconds": 150.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Okay, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.82,
      "end_seconds": 155.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.15,
      "end_seconds": 175.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.09,
      "end_seconds": 180.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.22,
      "end_seconds": 184.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "So, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.98,
      "end_seconds": 191.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.76,
      "end_seconds": 194.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.53,
      "end_seconds": 210.76,
      "duration_seconds": 15.23,
      "text": "Hmm, um, yes, low haemoglobin. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.69,
      "end_seconds": 220.8,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Right, so low haemoglobin is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 221.44,
      "end_seconds": 231.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse is 82 beats a minute, SpO2 98 percent on room air, blood pressure 128 over 78, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.01,
      "end_seconds": 233.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.11,
      "end_seconds": 238.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.15,
      "end_seconds": 243.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.97,
      "end_seconds": 262.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "The prostate feels smooth and enlarged with no hard areas."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.69,
      "end_seconds": 269.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.57,
      "end_seconds": 301.79,
      "duration_seconds": 18.22,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, this is probably benign prostate enlargement. I can't rule out a urine infection yet. There's nothing new for me to start or arrange today. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.44,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
